@startuml PDA_Sequence_Start_Then_Report
title PDA Happy Path — Start Job then Report Completion

actor "Line Operator" as Op
participant "PDA App\n(Android)" as App
participant "Scan SDK" as Scan
participant "Spring Boot API\n(NoOrderController)" as API
database "SQL Server\nPDA_NoOrder" as DB

== Login & context ==
Op -> App : open app / enter or scan employee ID
App -> Scan : read barcode (optional)
Scan --> App : employee code
App -> API : POST /api/login
activate API
API -> DB : lookup pda_user
DB --> API : user
API --> App : UserDto
deactivate API

Op -> App : select Line / MachineGroup / Machine\n(or scan device code)
App -> API : GET /api/lines , /api/procedures , /api/devices
activate API
API -> DB : read master / device context
DB --> API : lists
API --> App : Line / Procedure / Device DTOs
deactivate API

== Start job ==
Op -> App : enter/scan batch + drawing/procedure
App -> Scan : scan batch / drawing (optional)
Scan --> App : barcode payload
App -> API : POST /api/work/start
activate API
API -> DB : INSERT pda_work_start
DB --> API : ok
API --> App : success
deactivate API
App --> Op : start confirmed

== Report completion ==
Op -> App : report on same context\n(scan if needed)
App -> API : POST /api/work/report
activate API
API -> DB : INSERT pda_work_report\n(+ business checks vs latest start)
DB --> API : ok
API --> App : success
deactivate API
App --> Op : report confirmed

note over App, API
  Optional failure: validation / device mismatch
  → API returns error; PDA shows message.
end note

@enduml
